id: design.deadline
kind: design
title: deadline vs timeout
aliases: deadline, absolute deadline, deadline vs timeout
tags: design, timeouts, resilience
questions:
  - should you use a deadline or a timeout?
  - what breaks when you convert between them?
invariant: A deadline is an absolute point in time; a timeout is a duration from now, so only the deadline survives a retry without you re-arithmetic-ing it.
answer_30s: Use a deadline (absolute instant) when the budget must survive retries, restarts, or handoffs; use a timeout (relative) for a single bounded operation where the caller created the budget.
when_to_use:
  - propagating a budget across service hops
  - anywhere an operation may retry and the total time must not grow
avoid_when:
  - the operation is single-shot and the caller has no budget to propagate
related:
  - design.timeouts
  - rust.timeout
  - design.cascading-timeouts
sources:
  - https://sre.google/sre-book/
